[[924,359,"During the inquest I heard evidence that the jejunostomy feeding protocol in place at the time of Lee's admission was insufficient and, in part not followed. This on balance, likely contributed to his death.","insufficient jejunostomy feeding protocol",""],[2384,906,"The finding of poor nursing care and treatment that was possibly causative of Dave's death and the evidence of the treating consultant that such poor care raised a mortality risk for other patients","poor nursing care and treatment",""],[2385,906,"There was no evidence before the court that these concerns have been addressed and remedied","lack of evidence of remediation",""],[2550,964,"There appears to be a significant discrepancy between clinicians on the consenting procedure for the identical treatment of endoscopy","inconsistent consenting for endoscopy",""],[2551,964,"A 'sip test' to exclude aspiration was not performed, and there has been no evidence that this had been noted or remedied at the Trust","aspiration not excluded",""],[2552,964,"A doctor did not take action when viewing an endoscopy report which contained an indication of a possible dangerous complication","failure to act on complication warning",""],[2553,964,"Appropriate records were not kept, or were not properly transferred, by senior staff","inadequate record keeping",""],[3454,1302,"Derriford Hospital in Plymouth is the main acute hospital site managed by UHP NHS","patient pushing incidents on ward",""],[3455,1302,"patient who pushed Mary Pomeroy had been involved in a number of incidents where he had used physical force on staff members on the ward in February 2022.","untreated psychiatric symptoms leading to aggression",""],[3456,1302,"Pomeroy had been involved in a number of incidents where he had used physical force on staff members on the ward in February 2022. At","repeated physical aggression toward staff",""],[3457,1302,"Pomeroy should, on 3 March 2022, have been subject to enhanced observations of care -","lack of enhanced monitoring of high-risk patient",""],[3458,1302,"UHP NHS's RCA report had been incorrect to conclude that the type of incident that occurred on 3 March 2022 could not have been foreseen","inadequate risk assessment in RCA",""],[3459,1302,"lack of assessment and management of this patient's behaviour and needs materially contributed to the incident which led to Mary Pomeroy suffering injuries and led to her death","inadequate behavioural management",""],[3641,1373,"Although Mrs Tellam was under the care of Royal Cornwall Hospital and awaiting a post operation follow up, when clinical staff at Liskeard Community Hospital had concerns about a possible infection at the site of the surgery Mrs Tellam was taken to Derriford Hospital rather than to the orthopaedic team at the Royal Cornwall Hospital who had recently operated on her","transfer to wrong hospital for orthopaedic follow up",""],[3642,1373,"When Mrs Tellam had recovered from a chest infection she was transferred from Derriford to Liskeard Community Hospital for further rehabilitation rather than to the Royal Cornwall Hospital for follow up on the developing problems with the fixing metalwork at the site of the hip surgery","transfer to wrong hospital for hip surgery follow up",""],[3643,1373,"Decisions relating to the transfer of Mrs Tellam between Liskeard Community Hospital and Derriford Hospital did not give sufficient weight to continuity of clinical care","lack of continuity in clinical care during transfers",""],[8334,3186,"There was an error of omission in record keeping and in handover from critical care to surgery, and that this error likely contributed to Ian's death.","incomplete handover of critical care information",""],[8335,3186,"There was no entry in Ian's hospital notes to indicate the full extent of the critical incident of 5 June 2022.","missing documentation of critical incident",""],[8336,3186,"The error of omission was unexplained and has not been investigated by the NHS.","uninvestigated omission",""],[8337,3186,"The surgical and anaesthetic team had no reason to suspect a secondary brain injury. The team had no information on Ian's neurological status.","lack of neurological status information",""],[8338,3186,"Had the surgical and anaesthetic team known of the extent of the critical incident of 5 June, the operation would have been delayed and further tests and assessments undertaken.","delayed surgery due to missing information",""],[8339,3186,"The Trust had chosen not to accept this recommendation but at the time the Trust made that decision it was not aware of the extent and significance of the error of omission.","failure to implement handover recommendations",""],[9577,3651,"I am concerned that the Pathology Department remains significantly under resourced. I ask you please to:- (1) Review the Consultants staffing levels in the Pathology Department particularly those Consultants dealing with Thoracic work so as to ensure timely and accurate diagnosis of conditions at this regional centre","under resourced pathology department",""],[13294,5154,"Mr. Bradfield was not given his steroids on 2.12.13","steroid administration",""],[13295,5154,"Mr. Bradfield was not prescribed intravenous hydrocortisone on 4","intravenous hydrocortisone prescription",""],[13296,5154,"Mr. Bradfield was not put on a stress dose of steroids whilst in Derriford hospital","stress dose steroid administration",""],[13297,5154,"The awareness and training of staff on the issue of steroid management","staff awareness and training",""],[13298,5154,"The lack of a policy on the administration of steroids generally and their use in situations where a number of co - morbidities are present","absence of steroid administration policy",""],[13299,5154,"The training and awareness of staff on the meaning of * Nil by Mouth","staff awareness of Nil by Mouth",""],[13300,5155,"there are 44 radiologists working within the Trust","radiology staff shortages",""]]